The rest of the paper is structured as follows. Section 2 describes methods used in prior work for

hallucination detection and mitigation. Section 3 describes our proposed approach, CLAP, and the

methodology for ne-grained detection and mitigation. Section 4 evaluates CLAP against baselines.

Section 5 provides an analysis of out-of-distribution generalisation. Finally, we perform an ablation

study of the design in section 6 before concluding with a discussion on future work in section 7.

